---
import SectionHeader from './SectionHeader.astro';
---

<section class="section reveal section-glow" style="background:var(--bg-dark);border-top:1px solid var(--border-subtle)">
  <div class="glow-orb purple bottom-left"></div>
  <div class="glow-orb mint top-right"></div>
  <div class="container" style="position:relative;z-index:1">
    <SectionHeader
      label="Proof, not promises"
      title="Things you can <span class='gradient-text'>actually check</span>"
      subtitle="I do not have client testimonials or case study results to show you, because I have not done paid client work yet. So here is what is real, and you are welcome to verify any of it."
    />

    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr));gap:20px">
      <div class="glass" style="padding:28px 26px;border-radius:18px">
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-bottom:14px">
          <span style="padding:4px 11px;border-radius:999px;font-size:10px;font-weight:700;background:rgba(34,197,94,0.14);color:#4ade80;border:1px solid rgba(34,197,94,0.3)">LIVE PRODUCT</span>
        </div>
        <h3 style="font-size:18px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 10px;color:#fff">CookTwo</h3>
        <p style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-muted)">
          A membership and booking platform with a customer-facing app and a staff dashboard, built to run
          membership and class bookings. It is a real working system, not a concept. I would describe it
          honestly as a live product rather than a proven business.
        </p>
        <a href="https://cooktwo.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;color:#5EEAD4;text-decoration:none">
          See it running
          <svg width="15" height="15" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" /></svg>
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="glass" style="padding:28px 26px;border-radius:18px">
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-bottom:14px">
          <span style="padding:4px 11px;border-radius:999px;font-size:10px;font-weight:700;background:rgba(34,197,94,0.14);color:#4ade80;border:1px solid rgba(34,197,94,0.3)">RUNNING NOW</span>
        </div>
        <h3 style="font-size:18px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 10px;color:#fff">The website pipeline</h3>
        <p style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-muted)">
          The automated system that produces the free concept sites you see here. It only uses verified public
          information, refuses to invent contact details or testimonials, tracks image licensing, and checks
          every build on mobile before it goes anywhere near a human. It has produced dozens of builds — some
          of which I then had to fix, which is exactly why I do not call it fully autonomous.
        </p>
        <span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-muted);font-style:italic">The thing behind the free offer</span>
      </div>

      <div class="glass" style="padding:28px 26px;border-radius:18px">
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-bottom:14px">
          <span style="padding:4px 11px;border-radius:999px;font-size:10px;font-weight:700;background:rgba(34,197,94,0.14);color:#4ade80;border:1px solid rgba(34,197,94,0.3)">RUNNING NOW</span>
        </div>
        <h3 style="font-size:18px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 10px;color:#fff">The assistant on this site</h3>
        <p style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-muted)">
          The customer-service assistant answering questions in the corner of this page. It knows Byte
          Digital's own services, captures the details of anyone who wants to talk, and hands over to me
          rather than inventing an answer. It is a working demonstration of step three — which is why I am
          looking for a pilot business to build the real version for.
        </p>
        <span style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-muted);font-style:italic">Try it — bottom right</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="glass" style="margin-top:22px;padding:24px 26px;border-radius:16px;border-color:rgba(94,234,212,0.25);background:rgba(94,234,212,0.04)">
      <p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--text-secondary)">
        <strong style="color:#5EEAD4">Why there are no testimonials here.</strong> Most sites your competitors
        are showing you have invented results in them, because paying for real ones is awkward. I would rather
        start with less and let the work speak. If that makes me look less impressive than a competitor with a
        wall of made-up numbers, fine — you will find out who was right once you have seen the actual work.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
